  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centre for Development Finance Studies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to mobilize substantial private capital to drive sustainable economic growth, particularly in sub-Saharan Africa. The Centre for Development Finance Studies (CDFS) will conduct applied research, including comprehensive mapping and analysis of local capital markets infrastructure to identify barriers such as inadequate regulatory frameworks and insufficient investment instruments. The team will leverage their unique combination of experience in international capital markets and familiarity with local challenges in developing countries to develop blueprints for scalable financial solutions that support robust financial ecosystems. The project aims to develop prototypes for applied solutions in developing countries, focusing on integrating development finance with global capital markets. Additionally, the project will engage in advocacy by working with multilateral development banks, development finance institutions, institutional investors, regulators, and key policymakers through targeted technical workshops. This integrated approach aims to address local currency risk, accelerate local capital markets development, and drive the mobilization and optimization of financial resources.</narrative>
  </description>
